---
title: Junction — the API your models already describe — FrontierJS
description: Junction is the API layer for FrontierJS on Bun. A short service over a model gives you the endpoints, the live updates and the production defaults, and an effect runs only when the write has committed.
render: static
---
<!--
  The Junction page: the API realm, argued in five sections. Prerendered,
  no script beyond the layout's theme swatches. Same shape as
  routes/basecamp.mesa and routes/litestone.mesa; the shared structure is components/ProductFrame.mesa.

  ── Section contract ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Each section is a component in components/junction/, and its root is
  `<section id=… class="bc-section">` holding a `.container.stack`:

    p.eyebrow                       the topic's name
    h2                              the claim, in the reader's words
    p.lede                          one or two sentences, one idea
    .bc-split
      ul.bc-points > li             <strong>head.</strong> ONE or TWO sentences,
                                    3–4 of them; a point over four lines is cut
      figure.bc-proof               ONE proof: real schema lines, real output of
                                    a run, or a .flow of real steps, with a
                                    figcaption saying where it came from
    p.bc-more                       "Read more:" links into the repo docs

  Every claim and every code line is lifted from the package docs or code, or
  from a run, and is something that works TODAY. Junction is published to npm,
  so the page can say so, but a claim still needs a doc fence, a test or a run behind
  it. Direction is labeled as direction. No comparison with another ORM unless
  the cell was re-verified.
-->
